WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.680
Fieldnote five. A day in the fork.

2
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.410
What happens to a provider
change, and to upstream's change,

3
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.140
between midnight and an image digest?

4
00:00:17.658 --> 00:00:20.548
From an upstream update
to a candidate image.

5
00:00:20.778 --> 00:00:23.268
Upstream is regenerated at midnight.

6
00:00:23.418 --> 00:00:26.068
The cascade carries it into the workspace.

7
00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:27.508
A person approves.

8
00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:31.668
Every eligible commit gets an image
digest and a turn in the stack.

9
00:00:31.738 --> 00:00:34.548
And nothing here is a
merge you run by hand.

10
00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:41.236
A sync is a generated tree, plus one
pull request and one tracking issue.

11
00:00:41.786 --> 00:00:44.196
Upstream doesn't carry the Azure provider.

12
00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:50.266
The fork keeps it, so a sync brings
the community's changes without ever

13
00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:52.116
touching the Azure paths.

14
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:55.476
Upstream is never merged in as text.

15
00:00:55.706 --> 00:00:59.476
The generated commit lands through
a reviewed sync pull request.

16
00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:04.186
Then the cascade merges main
first, then fork_upstream,

17
00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:05.636
into the workspace.

18
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.190
The labels on the tracking
issue are the state:

19
00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:14.910
cascade-active, cascade-blocked,
cascade-failed,

20
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:20.830
validated. A blocked cascade runs again
after a provider change on fork_integration.

21
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.998
A failed one retries when
someone removes human-required.

22
00:01:27.258 --> 00:01:30.298
The integration pull request and the
version pull request are different pull

23
00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:33.578
requests. Validation
runs on pull requests,

24
00:01:33.578 --> 00:01:36.538
and on pushes to main
and fork_integration.

25
00:01:36.538 --> 00:01:39.258
It pushes a digest for
every eligible commit,

26
00:01:39.258 --> 00:01:42.378
and the stack is borrowed for
it before any release exists.

27
00:01:42.378 --> 00:01:47.428
Thirteen service forks work this
way, each in its own service's slot.

28
00:01:47.498 --> 00:01:51.668
And the image a merge to main pushes
is the one that slot follows next.

29
00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.654
Follow the two changes
from Fieldnote four.

30
00:01:56.654 --> 00:01:59.694
The sync pull request
brings upstream's change,

31
00:01:59.694 --> 00:02:03.384
generated. The cascade
compiles both together.

32
00:02:03.614 --> 00:02:06.664
A person approves the
integration pull request.

33
00:02:06.814 --> 00:02:11.304
Validation pushes a candidate digest,
and it gets a turn in the stack,

34
00:02:11.374 --> 00:02:13.464
which is what Fieldnote six follows.

35
00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:16.344
The cache fix and its unit tests are real;

36
00:02:16.414 --> 00:02:18.584
the acceptance run is illustrative.

37
00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.140
An easy mistake:

38
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.340
a release builds a fresh
image for the version tag.

39
00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:29.260
Validation already pushed an immutable
image for the release commit.

40
00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.660
The release workflow waits for that
image and adds the version tag to it.

41
00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.580
The bytes on the merge commit are
the bytes that get the version.

42
00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.900
To check, read the package's tags.

43
00:02:43.878 --> 00:02:45.088
So now you can say:

44
00:02:45.478 --> 00:02:48.928
a sync is a generated tree
and a reviewed pull request,

45
00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:51.728
and the cascade carries
it into the workspace.

46
00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.768
The labels on the tracking
issue are the state.

47
00:02:54.918 --> 00:02:59.158
And every eligible commit gets a
digest and a turn in the stack,

48
00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:01.568
before any release exists.

49
00:03:03.918 --> 00:03:07.688
Next: how does a candidate
image reach a running stack,

50
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:12.088
what proves it, and how is the
temporary test deployment restored?

